1
00:00:01,260 --> 00:00:08,020
Answer following questions below.

2
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:17,970
When was Sadako exposed to radiation?

3
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:26,550
A. When America dropped two atomic bombs on Japan.

4
00:00:26,930 --> 00:00:36,880
B. Ten years after America dropped bombs on Japan.

5
00:00:37,170 --> 00:00:45,680
C. Many years after America dropped bombs on Japan.

6
00:00:48,620 --> 00:01:03,750
Answer: A. Sadako was exposed to radiation when America dropped two atomic bombs on Japan.

7
00:01:04,170 --> 00:01:14,400
How did Sadako believe she would recover?

8
00:01:15,550 --> 00:01:25,350
A. She folded enough 100 paper cranes.

9
00:01:25,350 --> 00:01:35,420
B. She folded enough 644 paper cranes.

10
00:01:35,420 --> 00:01:44,400
C. She folded enough 1000 paper cranes.

11
00:01:48,240 --> 00:02:01,750
Answer: C. She folded enough 1000 paper cranes.

12
00:02:02,770 --> 00:02:15,440
What did children around the world do to show solidarity and sympathy for Sadako?

13
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:25,880
A. Write letters to ask about Sadako's health.

14
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:37,130
B. Fold thousands of paper cranes to send to Sadako.

15
00:02:37,460 --> 00:02:44,860
C. Raise money to build Sadako monument.

16
00:02:48,860 --> 00:03:04,080
Answer: B. Fold thousands of paper cranes to send to Sadako.

17
00:03:04,510 --> 00:03:20,570
What did children do to express their peace wish?

18
00:03:22,750 --> 00:03:46,000
Hiroshima students raised money to build monument to remember atomic bomb victims.

19
00:03:46,530 --> 00:03:58,910
The monument is engraved with lines expressing children's wish: this world forever peaceful.

